*Not to be confused with the Quetzalcoatl*

**Coatl** (/' *koən* /, Scripts) General Description

# Appearance

# Other Planes

# Powers and Abilities 
## Glide
Coatl folk have a heritage in the sky, using their limited feathers to glide through the air, though they cannot truly fly. With a leap, you can take to the air, gaining a flying speed equal to your speed. While flying in this way, you cannot gain altitude and you descend 1 foot for every 10 feet of horizontal movement. With the help of an updraft, however, you can retain your altitude.

## Featherworkers
Coatl communities often feature expert artisans who craft objects from coatl feathers. These artifacts include feathered objects like fans, but the featherworker can use feathers to adorn other things, such as shields, with the height of their art being the creation of headdresses and clothing. You have proficiency with a set of Artisan’s Tools unique to coatl culture: Feathercrafters’ Tools. Not only can you craft nonmagical objects for sale as you can with any artisan’s tool, but you may also use a featherworked object you have created as an arcane focus.
